From ec352cff66015c31b45bc89ebfdc97d176f8d923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 11:37:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] v4.6-gpu: GPU virtual time scheduling, KERNEL vtime
 boost, idle-start, deferred accounting, em dash fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>

v4.6-gpu: fix stats tree branch label alignment

The tree branch labels for lock contention and entity freed had too much
trailing padding, misaligning the value column.  Fixed to all be exactly
22 display characters wide (matching the regular label column).

Verifed with Python simulation that all value columns align at the same
position.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>

v4.6-gpu: fix Per-task EMA range spacing to align with value column

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>

v4.6-gpu: increase stats buffer to 2048 via kmalloc to prevent truncation

The previous stack-allocated 1024 byte buffer was too small for the
full output when Unicode box-drawing characters are used (each takes
3 bytes).  Two separator lines alone consume 422 bytes.  Switch to
kmalloc(2048) to eliminate the truncation and the frame size warning.

Also replace sizeof(buf) with a constant bufsz variable since buf is
now a heap pointer.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>

v4.6-gpu: revert to zero-allocation stack buffer, shorten separators

- Revert from kmalloc(2048) to char buf[1024] on stack -- zero allocation
- Shorten separator lines from 70 to 60 '─' characters so the full output
  (983 bytes) fits in 1024 bytes with null terminator
- Verified: no frame size warning, no memory leak, no UAF

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>

v4.6-gpu: rewrite stats handler with printf-style column format and | separators

Replace hand-padded string alignment with printf-style %-22s / %14s
column formatting.  Each row uses:

  | %-22s | %14s | %s

This guarantees perfect vertical alignment on every line regardless
of label length, eliminates the tree-branch offset bug, and makes
the output look like a proper table with | column separators.

Also add val_from_u64() helper with truncation safeguard: if the
comma-formatted value exceeds 14 characters (e.g. atomic counter
wrap), leftmost digits are cut and the rightmost 14 are kept so the
table column never shifts.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>

v4.6-gpu: rewrite stats with printf column format, +---+ borders, [section] headers

Per review team feedback, replace hand-aligned strings with printf-style
%-18s / %13s / %-26s column widths and | column separators:

  | %-18s | %13s | %-26s |
  +--------------------+---------------+----------------------------+

Column widths match exactly (67 chars), guaranteed by the format string
rather than manual space counting.  Also rename val_from_u64 to
fill_pretty_llu, change value column to 13 chars (fits uint32 max),
and use [ cpu ] / [ rt ] / [ gpu ] section headers.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
